###  https://www.example.org/ontoneo-u/ONTONEO_10000010
<https://www.example.org/ontoneo-u/ONTONEO_10000010> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf gufo:isObjectProperPartOf ;
                                                     rdfs:comment """In the original ontology, it is defined as \"A relationship that holds between two material entities, an injury and the entity injured\". However, is it formalized as a sub property of \"inheresIn\" - a relation that holds only between specific dependent continuants and the entities their bearers.

Injuries are defined as material entities, or the structural damage caused by a catastrophic external force. For this reason, we list them as (object) proper parts of the injured entity.""" ;
                                                     rdfs:label "injury of" .


