###  https://www.example.org/ontoneo-u/FMA_20192
<https://www.example.org/ontoneo-u/FMA_20192> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.example.org/ontoneo-u/BFO_0000028> ;
                                              rdfs:comment """Inherited from Foundational Model of Anatomy, an ontology that had its last version released in 04/24/2019.

The definitions of orifice, cavity and vestibules are all made with respect to a surrounding material entity - which leads one to view them as BFO:Site and not BFO:SpatialRegion. 

They are apparently specializations of Anatomical Space, imported from the Common Anatomy Reference Ontology - a deprecated ontology that had its concepts migrated to UBERON (for CARO and UBERON ontolgies, please refer to OBO Foundry).

It is necessary to clarify the motivation in OntONeo developers in importing conflcting concepts from different ontologies.""" ;
                                              rdfs:label "Vestibule" .


