                                              rdfs:comment """Inherited from Foundational Model of Anatomy (FMA), has as definition \"Anatomical structure, which is the developmental form of a vertebrate animal or any of its parts at any given time from fertilization of the egg by the sperm to parturition. Examples: embryo, embryonic structure, fetus, fetal heart.\"

According to Transformation Pattern #7, it is an Object.

Transformation respected the disjointness restriction with respect to immaterial entities.""" ;
                                              rdfs:label "Gestational structure" .


