                                                 rdfs:comment """Inherited from the Phenotype and Trait Ontology (PATO), it has as descriotion \"A quality which inheres in a continuant.\"

In the documentation, it elucidates in a comment the difference between relational and monadic qualities, and defines physical object quality as the exact synonym as \"monadic quality of a continuant\".

Being monadic means it concerns single individuals, thus being transformed, according to Transformation Pattern #9, to gUFO:Quality.""" ;
